::Practice Questions::
What is the data type of None in Python? 
{
= NoneType 
~ NullType 
~ NullValue 
~ Void
}

::Practice Questions::
What does a function return if it doesn't have an explicit return statement? 
{
~ An error 
~ 0 
= None
~ The last expression evaluated
}

::Practice Questions::
Which of the following is a valid use case for None in Python?  
{
~ Placeholder for uninitialized variables 
~ Default return value for functions 
~ Handling nullable database fields 
= All of the above
}

::Practice Questions::
You can use None as a default value for function arguments in Python. 
{
= True 
~ False
}

::Practice Questions::
None is considered a "falsy" value in Python, meaning it evaluates to False in boolean contexts. 
{
= True 
~ False
}

::Practice Questions::
You can assign a value other than None to the NoneType data type.
{
~ True
= False
}
